Relevant columns and why they matter  

• activities.activity_id : unique identifier for each measurement – needed for UUID construction and duplicate counting  
• activities.assay_id : lets us keep only results from the same assay and to count activities per assay (< 5)  
• activities.molregno : compound identifier – connects “activities” with compound‑level tables  
• activities.standard_type / activities.standard_units / activities.standard_relation / activities.standard_value : used to keep pairs that share the same standard_type, supply the numerical value and its relational sign ( =, <, >, … ) for “increase / decrease / no‑change” classification  
• activities.pchembl_value : potency on the –log scale; must be > 10  
• activities.potential_duplicate : must be < 2 duplicates in an assay (count value = '1')  

• compound_properties.molregno : key for joining to activities  
• compound_properties.heavy_atoms : filter to 10 – 15 heavy atoms; also the “max heavy atom count” field to report  
• compound_properties.full_molformula / mw_monoisotopic … : not strictly required but useful checks  

• compound_structures.canonical_smiles : needed for the hash‑based UUID (activity_id + canonical_smiles)  

• docs.doc_id : join from activities.doc_id to obtain publication metadata, keep newest (highest) id  
• docs.journal / docs.year / docs.first_page : required to synthesise the publication date (year, pseudo‑month, pseudo‑day by rank inside {journal, year})  

Key filter conditions to remember  

• compound_properties.heavy_atoms BETWEEN 10 AND 15  
• activities.pchembl_value > 10  
• activities.standard_value IS NOT NULL  
• per (assay_id, molregno) have COUNT(*) < 5  
• DUPLICATE check – COUNTIF(potential_duplicate = '1') < 2  

-----------------------------------------------------------------
Below are ten exploratory BigQuery SQL snippets (each capped with LIMIT 20) that build up from simple inspection to the more complex joins required for the final task.

```sql
-- 1. Inspect the distribution of heavy atom counts
SELECT DISTINCT CAST(heavy_atoms AS INT64) AS heavy_atoms, COUNT(*) AS n_compounds
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.compound_properties`
WHERE heavy_atoms IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY heavy_atoms
ORDER BY heavy_atoms
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. List compounds with 10‑15 heavy atoms and their pChEMBL activities >10
SELECT a.activity_id, a.assay_id, a.molregno, a.pchembl_value, cp.heavy_atoms
FROM  `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.activities`           AS a
JOIN  `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.compound_properties`  AS cp
ON    cp.molregno = a.molregno
WHERE cp.heavy_atoms BETWEEN 10 AND 15 
  AND CAST(a.pchembl_value AS FLOAT64) > 10
  AND a.standard_value IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Count how many activities each compound has in an assay
SELECT assay_id,
       molregno,
       COUNT(*) AS act_cnt
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.activities`
GROUP BY assay_id, molregno
HAVING act_cnt < 5
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Detect possible duplicate records inside each assay for a compound
SELECT assay_id,
       molregno,
       COUNTIF(potential_duplicate = '1') AS duplicate_rows
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.activities`
GROUP BY assay_id, molregno
HAVING duplicate_rows < 2
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Bring together activity and structure information
SELECT a.activity_id,
       a.assay_id,
       a.standard_value,
       s.canonical_smiles
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.activities`          AS a
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.compound_structures` AS s
USING (molregno)
WHERE a.standard_value IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Compute synthetic publication dates using window functions
WITH doc_rank AS (
  SELECT doc_id,
         journal,
         COALESCE(CAST(year AS INT64), 1970) AS yr,
         SAFE_CAST(first_page AS INT64) AS pg,
         PERCENT_RANK() 
           OVER (PARTITION BY journal, COALESCE(year, '1970')
                 ORDER BY SAFE_CAST(first_page AS INT64)) AS p_rank
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.docs`
  WHERE first_page IS NOT NULL AND journal IS NOT NULL
)
SELECT doc_id,
       yr AS pub_year,
       1 + CAST(FLOOR(p_rank*11) AS INT64)  AS pub_month,
       1 + CAST(FLOOR(p_rank*308) AS INT64) % 28 AS pub_day
FROM doc_rank
ORDER BY doc_id DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Join activities with docs to get the computed publication date
WITH doc_dates AS (
  SELECT doc_id,
         COALESCE(CAST(year AS INT64), 1970) AS yr,
         journal,
         SAFE_CAST(first_page AS INT64) AS pg,
         PERCENT_RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY journal, COALESCE(year,'1970')
                              ORDER BY SAFE_CAST(first_page AS INT64)) AS p_rank
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.docs`
)
SELECT a.activity_id,
       a.doc_id,
       dd.yr  AS pub_year,
       1 + CAST(FLOOR(dd.p_rank*11) AS INT64)               AS pub_month,
       1 + CAST(FLOOR(dd.p_rank*308) AS INT64) % 28         AS pub_day
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.activities` AS a
JOIN doc_dates AS dd
ON  dd.doc_id = a.doc_id
WHERE a.doc_id IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Pair two different molecules measured in the same assay & standard_type
SELECT
    a1.activity_id  AS act_id_1,
    a2.activity_id  AS act_id_2,
    a1.assay_id,
    a1.standard_type,
    a1.standard_value AS value_1,
    a2.standard_value AS value_2
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.activities` AS a1
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.activities` AS a2
  ON a1.assay_id = a2.assay_id
 AND a1.standard_type = a2.standard_type
 AND a1.molregno <> a2.molregno
WHERE a1.standard_value IS NOT NULL
  AND a2.standard_value IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Classify change direction between two standard values
SELECT
  act_id_1,
  act_id_2,
  CASE
    WHEN SAFE_CAST(value_1 AS FLOAT64) < SAFE_CAST(value_2 AS FLOAT64) 
         AND a1.standard_relation IN ('=', '<', '<=') 
         AND a2.standard_relation IN ('=', '>', '>=') THEN 'increase'
    WHEN SAFE_CAST(value_1 AS FLOAT64) > SAFE_CAST(value_2 AS FLOAT64) 
         AND a1.standard_relation IN ('=', '>', '>=') 
         AND a2.standard_relation IN ('=', '<', '<=') THEN 'decrease'
    WHEN SAFE_CAST(value_1 AS FLOAT64) = SAFE_CAST(value_2 AS FLOAT64) 
         AND a1.standard_relation = '=' 
         AND a2.standard_relation = '=' THEN 'no-change'
    ELSE 'uncertain'
  END AS change_class
FROM (
  -- reuse the pairing CTE created in query #8
  SELECT
      a1.activity_id  AS act_id_1,
      a2.activity_id  AS act_id_2,
      a1.standard_value AS value_1,
      a2.standard_value AS value_2,
      a1.standard_relation,
      a2.standard_relation
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.activities` AS a1
  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.activities` AS a2
    ON a1.assay_id = a2.assay_id
   AND a1.standard_type = a2.standard_type
   AND a1.molregno     <> a2.molregno
  WHERE a1.standard_value IS NOT NULL
    AND a2.standard_value IS NOT NULL
) AS paired
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Create MD5 based UUIDs from activity IDs and canonical SMILES
WITH act_struct AS (
  SELECT a.activity_id, s.canonical_smiles
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.activities`          AS a
  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.compound_structures` AS s
  USING (molregno)
  WHERE a.activity_id IN ('400977','794406') -- sample ids
)
SELECT 
  activity_id,
  MD5( TO_JSON_STRING(STRUCT(activity_id, canonical_smiles)) ) AS mmp_delta_uuid
FROM act_struct
LIMIT 20;
```

Each query incrementally explores or constructs pieces needed for the final answer: filtering on heavy atoms, counting assay occurrences, joining to structures and docs, synthesising publication dates, pairing activities, classifying potency change, and generating deterministic UUIDs.
